@page "/tables/advanced-table/reflow"

@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Switch
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.AdvancedTable.Components
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.AdvancedTable.Components.Columns

@{
    var widthPropertyName = nameof(AdvancedTableColumn<>.Width);
    var minimumWidthPropertyName = nameof(AdvancedTableColumn<>.MinimumWidth);
}

<h3>Column re-flow</h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    Flex columns — those without a <code>@widthPropertyName</code> — share out whatever space the table has,
    and they share it out again every time that space changes: a window resize, a dialog growing, a sidebar
    opening, a zoom step. Narrow the container below to watch it happen. Most of the containers here are capped
    at 900px, so they only follow the browser window once it goes under that; the <em>Always full width</em>
    sample is uncapped and follows it at every size.
</DescriptionBanner>

<div class="options">
    <div class="option">
        <label>Narrow container</label>
        <Switch @bind-Value="_narrow"/>
    </div>
</div>

<h3>All columns flex</h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    Three flex columns split the space equally and fill the container exactly, whatever width it has. The split
    is made at the same sub-pixel precision the browser lays the table out with rather than in whole pixels, so
    the columns land where they were already drawn and nothing shifts once the table has been sized.
</DescriptionBanner>

<div class="@GetContainerCssClass("all-flex")">
    <AdvancedTable ItemsProvider="_itemsProvider" MaximumHeight="300px">
        <Columns>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Key" Title="Key" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Key</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Value" Title="Value" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Value</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Timestamp" Title="Timestamp" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Timestamp</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
        </Columns>
    </AdvancedTable>
</div>

<h3>Always full width</h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    This container is not capped, so it tracks the browser window at every size. Drag the window edge and the
    columns follow it continuously — they are recomputed in the browser, so nothing waits on a round trip to
    the server. The switch above does not touch this one; the window is what sizes it.
</DescriptionBanner>

<div class="reflow-container full-width">
    <AdvancedTable ItemsProvider="_itemsProvider" MaximumHeight="300px">
        <Columns>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Key" Title="Key" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Key</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Value" Title="Value" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Value</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Quantity" Title="Quantity" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Quantity</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Timestamp" Title="Timestamp" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Timestamp</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
        </Columns>
    </AdvancedTable>
</div>

<h3>What re-flow leaves alone</h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    A column is only re-flowed while nobody has pinned it. <code>Id</code> declares
    <code>@widthPropertyName</code> and keeps that width for good. Drag any other column's right edge and it
    keeps the width you gave it too — from then on it is yours, and only the columns beside it go on sharing
    what is left. <code>Key</code> floors at a <code>@minimumWidthPropertyName</code> of <code>200</code>:
    narrow the container and it stops shrinking there. Its minimum plus <code>Id</code>'s declared width and the
    other two floors add up to more than the narrowed container, so the table outgrows it and scrolls
    horizontally.
</DescriptionBanner>

<div class="@GetContainerCssClass("mixed")">
    <AdvancedTable ItemsProvider="_itemsProvider" MaximumHeight="300px">
        <Columns>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Id" Title="Id (Width 100)" Width="100" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Id</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Key" Title="Key (min 200)" MinimumWidth="200" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Key</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Value" Title="Value" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Value</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Timestamp" Title="Timestamp" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Timestamp</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
        </Columns>
    </AdvancedTable>
</div>

<h3>Every column pinned</h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    With a <code>@widthPropertyName</code> on every column there is nothing left to re-flow, so the table
    keeps its own width and shows the container's background to the right of its last column. It does not
    stretch to the edge, and there is no filler column.
</DescriptionBanner>

<div class="@GetContainerCssClass("all-fixed")">
    <AdvancedTable ItemsProvider="_itemsProvider" MaximumHeight="300px">
        <Columns>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Id" Title="Id" Width="100" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Id</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Key" Title="Key" Width="160" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Key</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
            <AdvancedTableColumn Id="Value" Title="Value" Width="160" Resizeable>
                <CellContent>@context.Value</CellContent>
            </AdvancedTableColumn>
        </Columns>
    </AdvancedTable>
</div>
